# The kind lab, recorded from scratch on 2026-09-30 with cub kubara built from
# the handover-argobot-live-status branch (0.3.0-dev). It adds sections 5, 8 and
# 9 to the run of 2026-09-28: live status from argobot, and a stage gated on it.
#
# up.sh built a Kubara v0.15.0 platform (catalogs 3.0.0) on kind v0.31.0 with
# Kubernetes v1.35.0, on clusters named klab-hub and klab-spoke (KIND=klab), a
# hub called hub in stage dev and a spoke called spoke in stage prod. Kubara's
# bootstrap installed Argo CD 3.5.2 on the hub. run.sh then ran against a hosted
# ConfigHub organization with cub v0.6.8 and PREFIX=klab-0930-m2. handover.sh
# installed argobot v0.1.7 on the hub.
#
# up.sh took 9 minutes and run.sh 21. The lab directory is shown as
# ./kubara-lab. On kind, cert-manager is Degraded (Let's Encrypt refuses the
# example.com contact), traefik is Progressing (no load balancer), and the
# hub's argocd Application waits for an Ingress address.
#
# What to look for:
# - handover.sh step 6/6: argobot starts as the Targets' server worker, and
#   each of the 8 variant Spaces Argo CD delivers gets confighub.com/live-status
#   (section 3). Section 5 prints them.
# - Section 8: prod requires Released and Healthy. Straight after dev's release,
#   argobot still reports the release before it as Synced and Healthy, and a
#   dry run of the promotion to prod passes on that. check says dev does not
#   run its latest release yet. Once argobot reports the new release Synced and
#   Healthy, prod accepts it.
# - Section 9: an image that does not exist reaches dev. argobot reports dev
#   Degraded, and ConfigHub refuses the promotion to prod: "Variant 'hub' is not
#   healthy". The change is then aborted, demoted and dev released again.
#
# The same gap was measured with a real promotion, not a dry run, on an earlier
# lab the same day (PREFIX=klab-0930). Dev released an image that does not
# exist at 13:00:51 UTC, while argobot still reported the release before it:
#   {"syncStatus":"Synced","healthStatus":"Healthy","operationPhase":"Succeeded","revision":"sha256:aae35595572e...","observedAt":"2026-09-30T12:52:20Z"}
#   $ cub variant promote --change-order klab-0930-metrics-server-base/stale-test --target-stage prod --quiet
#   Promoting klab-0930-metrics-server-spoke into stage prod...
#   Upgraded 1 unit(s) behind their upstream
# It was accepted at 13:00:53. Argo CD synced the release at 13:01:16 and argobot
# reported Degraded at 13:01:55. The change was then aborted and demoted.
#
# argobot also tries to refresh an Application named after the Space on each
# release. Kubara names its Applications <cluster>-<service>, so it finds none:
#   [ERROR] argobot: sync of "klab-0930-metrics-server-hub" failed: patch Argo CD application
#   "klab-0930-metrics-server-hub" in namespace "argocd": applications.argoproj.io "klab-0930-..." not found
# run.sh refreshes the Application itself.

######## KIND=klab bash examples/kind-lab/up.sh


